hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17099","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Himyar al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Thabit ibn Ajlan narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Kathir al-Muharibi say: I heard Kharashah ibn al-Hurr say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will be after me a trial; the sleeper in it is better than the awake, and the sitter in it is better than the stander, and the stander in it is better than the runner. So whoever it reaches, let him walk with his sword to a rock and strike it until it breaks, then let him lie down for it until it passes as it passes."
